infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title One wrong word: except Exception vs bare except
  desc Since Python 3.8 CancelledError is a BaseException — the two clauses diverge exactly here
  compares
    - label except Exception (safe)
      children
        - label except Exception — safe since 3.8
          desc CancelledError is a BaseException, flies through
        - label Task unwinds, ends cancelled
          desc the canceller gets the unwind it is owed
        - label cancel() actually kills the task
          desc task.cancelled() is True, await is not lied to
        - label Shutdown gather() completes
          desc deploy finishes in the intended ~90 s
    - label bare except (bug)
      children
        - label bare except / except BaseException
          desc catches CancelledError, then loops again
        - label 32 immortal workers
          desc gather() can never return
        - label Shutdown hangs ~10 min to SIGKILL
          desc orchestrator loses patience and force-kills
        - label In-flight jobs double-processed
          desc redelivered after restart — duplicate emails
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f43f5e
